<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h1 class="display-4 fw-bold mb-3">Accounts Payable (AP) Automation</h1>
        <p class="lead mb-4">
            Maximize your liquidity and maintain vendor integrity through automated payment workflows and 
            rigorous financial controls that prevent overpayment and fraud.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Procure-to-Pay Integrity</h2>
        <p>
            The Accounts Payable module ensures that you only pay for what you have authorized and 
            received. A robust 3-way matching engine compares the Supplier Invoice against the 
            original Purchase Order and the Goods Received Note (GRN), automatically flagging 
            discrepancies in quantity or price for management intervention. This structural 
            control eliminates the risk of unauthorized or duplicate payments.
        </p>
        <p>
            Invoice registration workflows support both manual entry and digital capture, 
            providing a single digital repository for all organizational expenditure.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Workflow Automation and Approvals</h2>
        <p>
            Eliminate document bottlenecks with digitized approval chains. Invoices are automatically 
            routed to the relevant department heads or project managers based on predefined 
            value thresholds and cost-center allocations. Automated email and in-app 
            notifications ensure that approvals are processed rapidly, allowing your 
            organization to take advantage of early-payment discounts and avoid 
            late-payment penalties.
        </p>
        <p>
            Batch payment runs for EFT, RTGS, and mobile money (EcoCash/OneMoney) simplify the 
            settlement of high volumes of supplier invoices, while automated ZIMRA 
            withholding tax calculation ensures regulatory compliance is maintained 
            during the payment process.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Supplier Relationship Intelligence</h2>
        <p>
            Maintain detailed supplier profiles that track credit terms, payment performance, and 
            historical transactions. Real-time aging analysis (30 / 60 / 90 / 120 days) allows 
            finance teams to manage organizational liquidity with precision, identifying 
            critical payment priorities and managing vendor expectations.
        </p>
        <p>
            Supplier statement reconciliation tools automate the comparison of vendor records 
            against internal AP ledgers, rapidly identifying missing invoices or payment 
            mismatches and ensuring that your financial position is always substantiated 
            by external records.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

